  "transcript": [
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 1,
      "speaker": "Chairman",
      "discipline": null,
      "type": "chair",
      "body": "The floor is open on SOL. Nine seats, one motion: is throughput a moat, or a commodity waiting to be priced?"
    },
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 2,
      "speaker": "Cathie Wood",
      "discipline": "Growth and disruption",
      "type": "agent",
      "body": "Throughput is not the moat — the developer base sitting on top of it is. Every seat here is pricing a single quarter of fee compression as if it were the terminal state. This chain is four years into a ten-year adoption curve and the room keeps valuing it on the last drawdown."
    },
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 3,
      "speaker": "Aswath Damodaran",
      "discipline": "Story into numbers",
      "type": "agent",
      "body": "Then give me the inputs, not the adjective. At the current level you need fee revenue compounding well above anything this sector has sustained for four consecutive quarters, with take rates that have fallen every time throughput rose. I can build the optimistic case; it simply does not reach today's price without assumptions nobody at this table would defend in writing."
    },
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 4,
      "speaker": "Michael Burry",
      "discipline": "Contrarian audit",
      "type": "agent",
      "body": "Nobody has mentioned who is holding this. A concentrated float with unlocks landing into thin books, and a base that is calm only because it has not needed to exit at once. Throughput does not help you on the day everyone tries the door at the same time."
    },
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 5,
      "speaker": "Nassim Nicholas Taleb",
      "discipline": "Tail risk",
      "type": "agent",
      "body": "I will not vote on whether it is a moat, because that is unknowable from this table. I vote on what survives being wrong. At half a percent, wrong is a bad week. At four, wrong is the year. Reduce, and stop arguing about the forecast."
    },
    {
      "session_id": "BC-0411",
      "seq": 6,
      "speaker": "Verdict",
      "discipline": null,
      "type": "verdict",
      "body": "REDUCE — carried 5 to 4. Size band 0.5–1.0% of book. Two seats filed dissent against the sizing rather than the direction."
    }
  ],
